\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Hail to the Lord's Anointed;
\par Great David's greater Son
\par Hail, in the time appointed,
\par His reign on earth begun
\par He comes to break oppression,
\par To set the captive free,
\par To take away transgression,
\par And rule in equity.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He comes, with succour speedy,
\par To those who suffer wrong;
\par To help the poor and the needy,
\par And bid the weak be strong
\par To give them songs for sighing,
\par Their darkness turn to light,
\par Whose souls, condemned and dying,
\par Were precious in His sight.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. He shall come down like showers
\par Upon the fruitful earth
\par Love, joy, and hope, like flowers,
\par Spring in His path to birth
\par Before Him, on the mountains,
\par Shall peace the herald go;
\par And righteousness in fountains,
\par From hill to valley flow.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Kings shall fall down before Him,
\par And gold and incense bring;
\par All nations shall adore Him,
\par His praise all people sing;
\par To Him shall prayer unceasing
\par And daily vows ascend;
\par His kingdom still increasing,
\par A kingdom without end.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O'er every foe victorious,
\par He on His throne shall rest;
\par From age to age more glorious,
\par All-blessing and all-blest,
\par The tide of time shall never
\par His covenant remove;
\par His name shall stand for ever,
\par His changeless name of Love.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

